#question: milestone 4 dry run: time, memory per task and output size of step 02 on the 20 most expensive snap-99 galaxies
#criteria: every task exits 0; `done N/N failed 0` in each log; profile files < 1 MB; Maximum resident set size per task (py_tasks_*/task_*.log) noted
#cost: 1 job x 1 node, 20 tasks of 1 galaxy each (the largest), expected well under 1 h
#expect: if all 20 tasks exit 0 within 1 h and each profile file is < 1 MB, the per-galaxy cost (~35 s CPU, ~10 s of it ellipse fits) holds and the full campaign fits one node; a task near the 64 GB limit or > 5 min per galaxy means --mem/--time of diag_snap99 must be raised before submitting it
#view: view.json (scripts/write_view.py, run by hand or as a sidecar; reads logs/diag_snap*.log)
#by: claude (bars chat)
#next: set --mem and --time of diag_snap99 and diag_snap98 from the measured values, then submit diag_snap99
bars diag99_t20 --script $HOME/astro/gizmo/scripts/cluster/submit_python_tasks.slurm --env WORKDIR=$HOME/astro/clap/bars --mem 64 --time 01:00:00 -- $HOME/astro/scratch/bars/tasks/diag_snap99_t20.txt
